mental-model/mechanisms/execution-cycle.md:17:The Kernel has no scheduler of its own. The host that owns an in-process coordinator decides when to dispatch a `READY` Execution and when to fire the timers the Kernel reports due. A [wait](waits.md) whose deadline is already due when its Outcome is accepted, and for which no queued Event qualifies, expires inside that acceptance decision with no host fire ([registering a wait](waits.md#registering-a-wait), step 3). A live wait's deadline and an Execution deadline take effect only when the host fires them, so a host that never pumps timers never expires either of those.
