docs/development/017-known-limitations.md:96:| L-22 | Instant deadline enforcement for live waits and Execution deadlines. A wait left `WAITING` and an Execution deadline take effect only when the host calls `fireTimer` and the fire is accepted; a decision accepted earlier (an input, an Outcome, a dispatch) may win after the instant, and creation with a past Execution deadline is `READY`. A wait whose deadline is already due when it registers expires in that Outcome's own decision, with no fire (W-2). The host must pump `pendingTimers`/`fireTimer` | Acceptance order decides (W-9 case 4, CL-1); the binding has no internal scheduler; the owner chose fire-only enforcement | A host needs tighter bounds | K1.4 host or a K3 scheduler | [owner choice 01](work/K1.3/owner-choice-01.md); [K1.3 design 01](work/K1.3/design-01.md); [design check 01](work/K1.3/design-check-01.md) |
